{"title":"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 30","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b261e740e9145c114ee55b13c63b074927de0e53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 4x - x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"19\" />. Give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e669253c4e7faee3f83a492830f13b68c47b98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, consider the sequence defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/e/d4e18d21d38e22accf62e7947523d7b6e06be730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n} = f(x_{n-1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897470a282b6b85fa5221eacd41369b9a157f491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. \nFor how many real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e669253c4e7faee3f83a492830f13b68c47b98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> will the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b2d5144b4ca9b0152425a9cd7b45ccdb8f32657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0}, x_{1}, x_{2}, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"11\" /> take on only a finite number of different values?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1bebfb4cd2b4e6ae45e644da37b828405976b290.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{0}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{1 or 2}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{3, 4, 5 or 6}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{more than 6 but finitely many}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"672\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f179c1acaca157e8ed360c0fcd56e97fee4ac0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> gives the constant sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/2/1b2707534e557b43aa6c93a3530e6c9f4b8da87a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 0, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f9f75c79ed77a2dcf8b8a72fedb493c04b8b7b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) = 4 \\cdot 0 - 0^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"19\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a65b1e6ce8e8e1d2209b2c729772d7e3667c49f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(4)=0, x_{0} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> gives the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c08e846cc0ba2350546bd995965057c6f1f8f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 0, 0, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> with two different values. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f30ddcaee8ab383f7aff4ad680310002f3f7e1f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2) = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11cd7f3dfb91822bc781035a611264872c46c96f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> gives the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/a/a9a9b601c9620d2d1258793a200132d2f56eb828.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 4, 0, 0, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> with three values. In general, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/a/8fa9bff3e8b97a8cb5a1dcbd7b051a84bacc32c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0} = a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"10\" /> gives the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/8/2087811b66552fe1ccd77aef6c80378e530455fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n}, a_{n-1}, ... , a_{2}, a_{1}, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"157\" height=\"11\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> different values, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcf5664a462e70f0874b498c15a5c29d9f8f6fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a_{n+1}) = a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b47167574f79040ed1bfdfdcddc324dde9fb6dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0} = a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"12\" /> gives a sequence with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> different values. (It is easy to see that we could not have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8ea08f4119893b7d65c60f9416dacae20ac9e240.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1} = a_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c4874636654fe6121c11c428d34bd9451ef72d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i &lt; n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />.) Thus, it follows by induction that there is a sequence with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> distinct values for every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, as long as we can verify that there is always a real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36cfb07e4911e7b4f994b858f3d47604ddbee438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcf5664a462e70f0874b498c15a5c29d9f8f6fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a_{n+1}) = a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />. This makes the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d1302e73ece29d10218238af739577904f6f00a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" />. The verification alluded to above, which completes the proof, follows from the quadratic formula: the solutions to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f806a348b679d34429667d6fba8543cabe414e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a_{n+1}) = 4a_{n+1} - a_{n+1}^{2} = a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"228\" height=\"21\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/7910977a777494698c457926cfadd9344b78dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1} = 2 \\pm \\sqrt{4 - a_{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"19\" />. Hence if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3c6b5c0195f76ba1337335ec7ed6be478d522d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq a_{n} \\leq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36cfb07e4911e7b4f994b858f3d47604ddbee438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is real, since the part under the square root is non-negative, and in fact <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc5f0fcc2939d4d97fd8f63bf15d667ab8c9bfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq a_{n+1} \\leq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed71e8dc1b617b40b66cf3fd3021b607cd7543c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4-a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> will be between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the square root will be between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b966fc9bf6e807dfd41ffcb6c27508c1e1652c14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\pm$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> something between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives something between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Finally, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aaa92b0d68c662a3fae07c9a7ebb2109c2305fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1} = 0 \\leq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />, it follows by induction that all terms satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3c6b5c0195f76ba1337335ec7ed6be478d522d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq a_{n} \\leq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />; in particular, they are all real.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME\" title=\"1988 AHSME\">1988 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1988 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1988\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016230645\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 290/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2462/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 157/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8359/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.075      1 -total\n 54.92%    7.181      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 43.48%    5.685      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13691:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016230645 and revision id 92426. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}